      "summary": "The biggest risks are permission and supply, not demand — ADAFSA's farm-activity rules do not name ostriches, farm activities are open to farm owners or licensed establishments (so a partnership on an Emirati-owned farm is the realistic route, and ADAFSA's new Nama programme is pushing underused Al Ain farms into agri-tourism), live birds from South Africa have been banned since July 2019 with no published lifting found, and an established ostrich farm (Ostrich Oasis, ~2,000 birds, 75 t meat/yr) already operates in Al Ain; visitor economics work only in a ~7-month cool season.",
